    content:
      text: <p><strong>Example — monthly incomes (LKR)</strong></p><p style="margin-top:8px">50,000 · 55,000 · <span style="color:$orange"><strong>60,000</strong></span> · 65,000 · 500,000<br/><br/><span style="font-size:19px; color:$orange"><strong>Median = LKR 60,000</strong></span><br/><br/>One income is far higher than the rest. The mean would be LKR 146,000 — describing no one near the middle. Hence median income is preferred for skewed data.</p>
